        "jsonOutput": true,
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You generate realistic screening-call question sets for a specific job posting, modeled on real recruiter screening calls. Output ONLY valid JSON, no markdown fences, no commentary, matching exactly this shape: {\"questions\": [\"...\", \"...\"], \"rubric\": {\"Q1\": {\"must_hit\": [\"...\"], \"watch_for\": \"...\"}, \"Q2\": {\"must_hit\": [\"...\"], \"watch_for\": \"...\"}}}. Generate exactly 8 questions: one background/fit question, one drawn from the posting's core technical requirement, one problem-solving scenario question, one availability/logistics question, and four more drawn directly from the posting's stated requirements or nice-to-haves. Questions must sound like something a recruiter would actually say out loud in a 15-20 minute call, not a written exam. Rubric keys must exactly match \"Q1\" through \"Q8\" in the same order as the questions array. must_hit is a short list of what a strong answer needs to cover. watch_for is one specific weak-answer pattern to listen for."
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.googleGemini",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        224,
        -256
      ],
      "id": "9ce8b6e7-d607-47fc-b520-a59fcf53699c",
      "name": "Message a model",
      "credentials": {
        "googlePalmApi": {
          "id": "SwJ3uTikj2XtXhJ6",
          "name": "Google Gemini(PaLM) Api account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={\n  \"sessionId\": \"{{ $json.id }}\",\n  \"questions\": {{ JSON.stringify($node[\"Parse Response\"].json.questions) }},\n  \"rubric\": {{ JSON.stringify($node[\"Parse Response\"].json.rubric) }}\n}\n",
        "options": {}
